<%# The privacy policy. #682.

    Both assistant directories ask for a link to one, and Claude's will not list a connector
    without it. legal/privacy.md was the draft; this is the published text, and the draft now
    points here so there is one copy to keep true.

    Most of it is a description of what the app does, checked against the code rather than
    taken from a template, which means it goes stale the moment the behaviour changes. Two
    sentences were corrected on the way here because the draft promised more than the app
    does: there is no delete-my-account button, so deletion is by email, and assistant activity
    logs are never pruned, so they are kept as long as the account rather than for a period
    nobody implemented.

    Who runs it and how to reach them come from PRIVACY_OPERATOR in app.rb. The route serves
    this page only once all three are filled in, so it can never go out saying "[ADDRESS]". %>
<div class="<%= page_style(:reading) %> space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-700">
  <h1 class="serif text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="text-gray-500">Last updated: <%= PRIVACY_UPDATED %></p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    tectonic plates is run by <strong><%= PRIVACY_OPERATOR[:name] %></strong>,
    <%= PRIVACY_OPERATOR[:address] %>. For anything in this policy, including a request to see or
    delete your data, write to <strong><%= PRIVACY_OPERATOR[:email] %></strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">What we store</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Your account.</strong> An email address and a bcrypt hash of your password. We never
    store the password itself and cannot recover it, only reset it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Your training.</strong> Sessions, sets, exercises, loads, rep counts, RPE ratings,
    training maxes, goals, your plate inventory and bar weight, your time zone, and any notes you
    write on a session or a movement. This is the substance of the service and the reason to have
    an account.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Assistant activity.</strong> If you connect an AI assistant, we record each tool call
    it makes on your behalf: which tool, when, whether it succeeded, <strong>and the arguments it
    was given</strong>. That means the contents of a write (a weight, a rep count, a note) appear
    in that log. It exists so that a change you did not expect can be traced to the call that
    made it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What Withings sends, if you connect it.</strong> Only if you connect a Withings
    account, and only what Withings holds: your weight and body composition (lean mass, fat mass,
    fat percentage, muscle mass, hydration, bone mass), the heart rate taken with a measurement,
    how long you slept and over what window, the activities your watch recorded with their heart
    rate and calories, and the watch&rsquo;s heart rate over each session you match to one of its
    recordings. Weights you type into the Withings app are included. We only read from Withings
    and never write anything back. Disconnecting stops any further reading.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Where you arrived from.</strong> When you create an account we record which website or
    link you arrived from: the referring site&rsquo;s name only (for example www.reddit.com, never
    the page or anything you searched for), any <code>ref</code> or <code>utm_source</code> tag on
    the link, and the first page you opened here. It is held in your session cookie until you sign
    up, then saved with your account, so we can tell which places people find us through. It is
    never shared.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Nothing else.</strong> We do not ask for your name, date of birth, location or payment
    details, and we have nowhere to put them.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">What we do not do</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
    <li>We do not sell your data.</li>
    <li>We do not use your training data to train machine-learning models.</li>
    <li>We do not share it with advertisers, and there is no advertising on the service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    One session cookie, so that being signed in survives loading the next page, and an optional
    &ldquo;remember me&rdquo; token if you ask to stay signed in. That is all. There is no consent
    banner because there is nothing to consent to: see Fathom below.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Who else handles it</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
    <li><strong>Render</strong> (United States, Oregon) hosts the app and the database, so it holds everything above.</li>
    <li><strong>Fathom Analytics</strong> counts page views, referrers and a few named actions (an account created, a set completed), in aggregate. It is cookieless and builds no profile of you across sites.</li>
    <li><strong>Sentry</strong> receives error reports: the exception and where in the code it happened. It is set up not to send request headers or IP addresses. An error message could in principle contain a value you entered; we do not send them on purpose and do not look for them.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> receives your email address when we send you a confirmation link or a password reset.</li>
    <li><strong>Withings</strong> receives nothing from us. We only read from it, and only if you connect your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Your AI assistant&rsquo;s operator</strong>, if you connect one, handles whatever you say to it and whatever it reads from your account, under its own privacy policy. We see the tool calls it makes, not what you said to it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    For as long as you have an account, assistant activity logs included. To delete your account
    and everything in it, write to <strong><%= PRIVACY_OPERATOR[:email] %></strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Whatever your jurisdiction gives you, and at minimum: you can ask for a copy of everything we
    hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for it to be deleted. Write to
    <strong><%= PRIVACY_OPERATOR[:email] %></strong>. We will respond within 30 days.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in the UK or EU, the lawful basis for storing your training data is performance of
    the contract between us (the service does not work without it), and for analytics and error
    reporting, our legitimate interest in the service working and improving.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Where your data lives</h2>
  <p>
    On servers in the United States (Oregon). If you are outside the US, using the service means
    your data is transferred there.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Security</h2>
  <p>
    Passwords are hashed with bcrypt and every page is served over HTTPS. Your account is reached
    either with your password or with a token you granted to an assistant, and you can revoke any
    of those at any time from your connections page. We are a small operation and cannot promise a
    breach will never happen. If one does, we will tell affected people by email.
  </p>

  <h2 class="<%= heading_style(:section) %> pt-4">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, we will email the address on your account before the change
    takes effect.
  </p>
</div>
